Program Flow

The user enters the student name and subject. The user then enters the grades for the 
Performance Task, Quiz, and Exam. When the Evaluate Grade button is clicked, the program validates the grade inputs using double.
TryParse. The valid grades are stored in the List<double> generic collection. 
The program then processes the values inside the List to calculate the average, lowest grade, and highest grade. 
After the calculation is completed, the GradeEvaluated event is triggered. 
The GradeEvaluationHandler delegate passes the student information and calculated results to the DisplayGradeResult method. 
Finally, the application displays the student's grade evaluation, 
including the subject, average, lowest grade, highest grade, and whether the student passed or failed.
